review_comments:
iterating over a map here results in the warnings being in a non-deterministic order

if in the loop, we append warnings in the order evaluated, and separately track which pods they apply to, at the end, we can prefix the warnings with the applicable pod names:
```
if !r.Allowed {
  reason := r.ForbiddenReason()
  podNames, seen := warningsPodsMap[reason]
  if !seen {
    podWarnings = append(podWarnings, reason)
  }
  warningsPodsMap[reason] = append(podNames, pod.Name)
  ...
}
...

for _, podWarning := range podWarnings {
  warnings = append(warnings, warningWithPodNames(podWarning, warningsPodsMap)
}
```
